From: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 14:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: rtl8365mb: let the SerDes PLL settle after the data-path reset

The vendor DW8051 firmware waits ~98 ms after the BMCR data-path reset
(constant SGMII_TIMEOUT_98MS in Sgmii_Init[]) before any further SerDes
register access, giving the SerDes PLL and analog front-end time to
settle. Without the wait the SGMII link on the RTL8367S can come up
half-alive on cold boot: carrier up and RX passing traffic, TX
permanently dead (measured on a TP-Link Archer AX55 v1, IPQ5018).

Suggested-by: mietekn (OpenWrt forum, reduce-number-of-drivers-for-rtl8367s #72/#106)
Signed-off-by: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>

Adapted to skip family D (RTL8367S-VB): that family takes a dedicated
SerDes setup path (rtl8367d_pcs_config(), reached by an early return a
little further down in rtl8365mb_pcs_config()) with its own timing.
Inserting this wait ahead of that branch was measured, on the Mercusys
MR80X v5 (RTL8367S-VB, family D SDS13 tuning), to leave the CPU port
receiving nothing from the switch - carrier and TX fine, RX stuck at
zero packets on the conduit for the whole uptime - while family C
boards (this fix's original target) are unaffected either way, since
they never reach this code path at all for family D. Gating the wait on
family keeps the original fix intact for family C and avoids the
regression on family D.

Signed-off-by: Fabiano Tassotti <fabianotassotti@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb_main.c
@@ -1405,6 +1405,19 @@ static int rtl8365mb_pcs_config(struct p
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	if (rtl8365mb_get_family(priv) != RTL8365MB_FAMILY_D) {
+		/* The vendor DW8051 firmware waits ~98 ms after the data-path
+		 * reset (SGMII_TIMEOUT_98MS in Sgmii_Init[]) for the SerDes PLL
+		 * and analog front-end to settle before any further SerDes
+		 * register access. Without the wait the link can come up
+		 * half-alive on cold boot: carrier and RX fine, TX permanently
+		 * dead. Family D takes its own dedicated SerDes setup path
+		 * (see the early return to rtl8367d_pcs_config() below) with
+		 * its own timing, so it is skipped here.
+		 */
+		usleep_range(98000, 98500);
+	}
+
 	/* Keep SGMII in-band autonegotiation disabled: the link parameters are
 	 * forced from rtl8365mb_pcs_link_up() instead.
 	 */
